From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci-theme-bootstrap: header indicators on phones
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On screens up to 854 px the indicators in the header (automatic
refresh, unsaved changes) were limited to 20% of the header width, so
every indicator wrapped to two or three lines and the header grew
higher. Without the flex limit the indicators take the width of their
text; checked in Chromium at 390 px: the indicator column is 141 px
instead of 102 px and the header 55 px instead of 67 px high.

The same change is in LuCI master.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Uo9XQuT7u6ShTYdi2S3Anq
---
 htdocs/luci-static/bootstrap/mobile.css | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/htdocs/luci-static/bootstrap/mobile.css b/htdocs/luci-static/bootstrap/mobile.css
index c6d02b22..435e46b4 100644
--- a/htdocs/luci-static/bootstrap/mobile.css
+++ b/htdocs/luci-static/bootstrap/mobile.css
@@ -279,7 +279,6 @@ header h3 a, header .brand {
 	}
 
 	header .pull-right {
-		flex: 0 1 20%;
 		display: flex;
 		flex-direction: column;
 		padding: 0;
-- 
